Tell the audio processing its output is unused only when no channel sends sound

WebRtcVoiceSendChannel::MuteStream told the engine's one audio processing that its output
will be muted when all of THAT channel's send streams were muted. With unified plan every
audio section has a send channel of its own (a call's voice and a shared screen's sound,
one for each connection), so the channel touched last decided for all of them: a
connection closed while another one kept sending the microphone stopped its voice sender
(AudioRtpSender::ClearSend, SetAudioSend(ssrc, false), MuteStream(ssrc, true), "all 1 of
1 muted") and the processing took its output for unused. With
minimize_processing_for_unused_output (on unless WebRTC-MutedStateKillSwitch) it then
passed the microphone through untouched: no echo cancelling, no noise suppression and no
gain control, until some audio sender got a track again (a shared screen's sound starting
to go out to a watcher), which turned all three on in the middle of the call.

The engine now keeps the send streams that send sound, of every channel, by channel and
ssrc (on the worker thread, where every channel calls it), and tells the processing its
output will be muted only while there is none. A stream that goes (RemoveSendStream,
also as its channel goes) leaves the set, telling the processing only if it was the last
one sending. Channels never outlive the engine (the connection context holds it until
every connection is gone). Tested by the wrapper's test/voice_engine_muted.test.cc
(WebRTC's own webrtc_voice_engine_unittest.cc no longer builds since 0002 changed the
engine's constructor).

diff --git a/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.cc b/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.cc
index e6312c2..fba1984 100644
--- a/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.cc
+++ b/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.cc
@@ -842,6 +842,36 @@ AudioProcessing* WebRtcVoiceEngine::apm() const {
   return apm_.get();
 }
 
+void WebRtcVoiceEngine::SetSendStreamMuted(const void* channel,
+                                           uint32_t ssrc,
+                                           bool muted) {
+  RTC_DCHECK_RUN_ON(&worker_thread_checker_);
+  const std::pair<const void*, uint32_t> stream(channel, ssrc);
+  if (muted) {
+    unmuted_send_streams_.erase(stream);
+  } else {
+    unmuted_send_streams_.insert(stream);
+  }
+  AudioProcessing* ap = apm();
+  if (ap) {
+    ap->set_output_will_be_muted(unmuted_send_streams_.empty());
+  }
+}
+
+void WebRtcVoiceEngine::ForgetSendStream(const void* channel, uint32_t ssrc) {
+  RTC_DCHECK_RUN_ON(&worker_thread_checker_);
+  // A stream that sent nothing changes nothing; the last one that sent sound
+  // going leaves nothing sending.
+  if (unmuted_send_streams_.erase(std::make_pair(channel, ssrc)) == 0 ||
+      !unmuted_send_streams_.empty()) {
+    return;
+  }
+  AudioProcessing* ap = apm();
+  if (ap) {
+    ap->set_output_will_be_muted(true);
+  }
+}
+
 AudioState* WebRtcVoiceEngine::audio_state() {
   RTC_DCHECK_RUN_ON(&worker_thread_checker_);
   RTC_DCHECK(audio_state_);
@@ -1698,6 +1728,8 @@ bool WebRtcVoiceSendChannel::RemoveSendStream(uint32_t ssrc) {
   }
 
   it->second->SetSend(false);
+  // Fogata: no longer counted as sending sound (WebRtcVoiceEngine).
+  engine()->ForgetSendStream(this, ssrc);
 
   delete it->second;
   send_streams_.erase(it);
@@ -1821,14 +1853,9 @@ bool WebRtcVoiceSendChannel::MuteStream(uint32_t ssrc, bool muted) {
   // This implementation is not ideal, instead we should signal the AGC when
   // the mic channel is muted/unmuted. We can't do it today because there
   // is no good way to know which stream is mapping to the mic channel.
-  bool all_muted = muted;
-  for (const auto& kv : send_streams_) {
-    all_muted = all_muted && kv.second->muted();
-  }
-  AudioProcessing* ap = engine()->apm();
-  if (ap) {
-    ap->set_output_will_be_muted(all_muted);
-  }
+  // Fogata: all the channels of the engine, not only this one's streams (see
+  // WebRtcVoiceEngine::unmuted_send_streams_).
+  engine()->SetSendStreamMuted(this, ssrc, muted);
 
   return true;
 }
